From ed0e79f629805b20551e7dde33ea8e2091fd69b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:30:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add duration tracking for timed exercises
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Planks, dead hangs, wall sits and loaded carries are held for time, not
counted in reps. An exercise now carries mode:"reps" (default) or
mode:"duration"; timed sets store `duration` in seconds instead of `reps`.
Weight, RPE, rest, supersets and skip behave identically, so a weighted
plank logs its added load the same way a squat does.

Logging: the reps spinner is replaced by a hold-time picker with a live
stopwatch — start it, hold, tap stop and the elapsed time fills the field,
which is the natural flow when you don't know the number until you drop.
Quick chips offer the target, last session's hold and common times. A blank
field carries the previous set's hold forward, mirroring weight.

Existing data needs no migration: mode is inferred from the exercise name
(narrowly, so Hang Clean stays a reps lift) and from the starter templates'
reps:"45s" form. Only that explicit form counts as a hold — a bare rep
count is never read as seconds.

Timed work now contributes to volume and muscle stimulus instead of
counting as zero, via a time-under-tension rep-equivalent (~3s per rep).
History editors, session summaries, progress views and the history CSV
(new Duration column) all render and round-trip holds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
