Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Setup notes previously existed but were only editable in the program
editor and only visible while an exercise was active — so a rack pin
discovered to be a hole off could not be corrected where you noticed it.
The in-session note is now tappable: it opens in place, and the edit is
written back to the program day (debounced) so it is right next time.
Collapsed exercises show their setup read-only, so gear can be spotted
while scanning ahead. Freestyle sessions edit session-only, since there
is no program day to persist into.

Goals could only target weight x reps, which a timed exercise can never
satisfy — a plank goal sat permanently unachieved. Goals now take either
form: a REPS / HOLD toggle in the goal editor, inferred from the exercise
name and overridable by hand. Hold goals treat weight as optional so a
pure bodyweight target is expressible, progress tracks time held rather
than load moved, and achievement compares hold length (plus added weight
when set). Rep goals are untouched.

